CLAIMED FINDING (d): the README example does not run as written under Node. packages/kit/README.md lines 38-50 give the example under 'How to use it' and name no way to run it. I pasted it into a file, added only what the example leaves out (a Playwright page and a `tokens` value), and ran it with Node 22.

File scratch/readme.mjs:
import { chromium } from 'playwright';
import { KIT_RULES, grade, receipt, receiptText, repairPlan, designId } from '@refraction/kit';
import * as checks from '@refraction/kit/src/page-checks/index.js';
const browser = await chromium.launch();
const page = await browser.newPage();
await page.goto('file://' + process.cwd() + '/packages/kit/fixtures/good.html');
const tokens = { '--ink': '#1a1a1a' };
// In a browser page (Playwright): send each check into the page as text, so that it runs there.
const findings = [];
for (const fn of Object.keys(checks)) findings.push(...await page.evaluate(`(${checks[fn]})(document)`));

console.log(grade(findings, KIT_RULES));
console.log(repairPlan([findings], KIT_RULES));
console.log(receiptText(receipt(findings, KIT_RULES)));
console.log(designId(tokens));
await browser.close();

Command: node scratch/readme.mjs

CLAIMED FINDING (d): the README example crashes even where its imports resolve. README lines 42-44: "const findings = [];\nfor (const fn of Object.keys(checks)) findings.push(...await page.evaluate(`(${checks[fn]})(document)`));". The loop calls tokenFit with no tokens. README line 52 says "`tokenFit` takes a second argument, the design's tokens", but the example does not give it, and the example also reads a variable `tokens` that it never defines.

File scratch/readme.t.ts (the example inside a Vitest test, so that the imports resolve):
import { chromium } from 'playwright';
import { it } from 'vitest';
import { KIT_RULES, grade, receipt, receiptText, repairPlan, designId } from '@refraction/kit';
import * as checks from '@refraction/kit/src/page-checks/index.js';
it('README example, as written', async () => {
  const browser = await chromium.launch();
  const page = await browser.newPage();
  await page.goto('file://' + process.cwd() + '/packages/kit/fixtures/good.html');
  const tokens = { '--ink': '#1a1a1a' };
  try {
    const findings = [];
    for (const fn of Object.keys(checks)) findings.push(...await page.evaluate(`(${checks[fn]})(document)`));
    console.log(grade(findings, KIT_RULES));
    console.log(repairPlan([findings], KIT_RULES));
    console.log(receiptText(receipt(findings, KIT_RULES)));
    console.log(designId(tokens));
  } finally { await browser.close(); }
});

Command: npx vitest run --config scratch/vitest.config.ts scratch/readme.t.ts

CLAIMED FINDING (b): followed the README example with the one repair a user would make (tokenFit given {}), at Playwright's default window (1280 by 720), on packages/kit/fixtures/good.html. The receipt reports the 320-pixel floor as held although nothing was measured at 320 pixels. The rule record says (packages/kit/src/data/neuro.ts line 25) "At a width of 320 pixels the page needs no sideways scrolling." with appliesWhen "The checker sets the window to 320 pixels wide before it measures." The check does not set the width and does not refuse to answer at another width; it answers 'holds'. See also USR-4 for a page that is plainly too wide.

File scratch/readme2.t.ts:
import { writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import { chromium } from 'playwright';
import { it } from 'vitest';
import { KIT_RULES, grade, receipt, receiptText, repairPlan } from '@refraction/kit';
import * as checks from '@refraction/kit/src/page-checks/index.js';
it('README example with tokenFit given an empty token set, at the default window', async () => {
  const browser = await chromium.launch();
  const page = await browser.newPage();
  await page.goto('file://' + process.cwd() + '/packages/kit/fixtures/good.html');
  const findings: never[] = [];
  for (const fn of Object.keys(checks)) findings.push(...await page.evaluate(`(${(checks as Record<string, unknown>)[fn]})(document, {})`) as never[]);
  const own = KIT_RULES.filter((r) => r.check.kind !== 'person' && r.sources.every((s) => s.basis === 'builder' && /judgment/.test(s.title)) && r.evidence !== 'expert-opinion').map((r) => `${r.id} (${r.evidence})`);
  writeFileSync('scratch/readme2-out.txt', [JSON.stringify(page.viewportSize()), JSON.stringify(grade(findings, KIT_RULES)), JSON.stringify(repairPlan([findings], KIT_RULES)), receiptText(receipt(findings, KIT_RULES)), 'records whose only source is the builder\'s judgment and whose grade is not expert-opinion: ' + own.join(', ')].join('\n\n') + '\n');
  await browser.close();
});

